          "role": "user",
          "content": "How do Docker containers work?",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T17:59:37.521078+00:00"
        },
        {
          "role": "model",
          "content": "### \ud83d\udc33 Docker & Containerization Essentials\n\nDocker packages an application and its dependencies into a standardized unit called a **container**.\n\n**Core Concepts:**\n- **Dockerfile:** Recipe for building an immutable image.\n- **Image:** Read-only template with runtime, libraries, and code.\n- **Container:** Running instance of an image in isolated user space.\n- **Volume:** Persistent data storage decoupled from container lifecycle.\n\n```dockerfile\n# Production Python Dockerfile\nFROM python:3.12-slim\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\nCOPY . .\nCMD [\"uvicorn\", \"app.main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8000\"]\n```",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T17:59:37.521078+00:00"
        },
