        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "Explain FastAPI dependency injection",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T18:13:51.544256+00:00"
        },
        {
          "role": "model",
          "content": "### \u26a1 Mastering FastAPI\n\nFastAPI is a modern, high-performance web framework for building APIs with Python based on standard Python type hints.\n\n**Key Architectural Advantages:**\n- **High Performance:** On par with NodeJS and Go (powered by Starlette and Uvicorn).\n- **Automatic Data Validation:** Powered by Pydantic v2.\n- **Interactive Swagger Docs:** Automatically served at `/docs`.\n- **Dependency Injection:** Modular, testable services using `Depends()`.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Depends, HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass Item(BaseModel):\n    name: str\n    price: float\n\n@app.post('/items')\nasync def create_item(item: Item):\n    return {'message': f'Created {item.name}', 'price': item.price}\n```",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-19T18:13:51.544256+00:00"
        }
